# Default owners: repo maintainer + the review authority.
# (2026-10-14 audit: repo had no CODEOWNERS, templates, or tags.)
#
# WHY TWO OWNERS ON `*`:
# `required_approving_review_count: 1` alone is satisfied by ANY approval,
# including a bot's. Measured 2026-10-25: PRs #157 and #158 merged on an
# `APPROVED` from `sourcery-ai`, with no human review at all. Requiring CODE
# OWNER reviews closes that: an app's approval does not satisfy it.
#
# `@branben` is listed so the file is honest about ownership, but GitHub does
# not count an author's own approval on their own PR — so for PRs authored by
# @branben the effective required reviewer is @luna-whymage.
* @branben @luna-whymage

# CI and security gates — require an explicit human review
.github/workflows/ @branben @luna-whymage

# Privacy-sensitive data (must never contain PII / home paths)
data/last_run.json @branben @luna-whymage
